  "model_id": "noaa-rrfs-ens",
  "model_name": "NOAA RRFS ENS",
  "description_summary": "This dataset is an archive of past and present RRFS ensemble forecasts, optimized for spatial (map) access patterns. Forecasts are identified by an initialization time (`init_time`) denoting the start time of the model run, and step forward hourly along the `lead_time` dimension out to 60 hours. Each forecast has six members along the `ensemble_member` dimension: member 0 is the deterministic RRFS forecast and members 1 to 5 are perturbed.\n\nThis dataset uses the native RRFS Lambert Conformal Conic projection, with spatial indexing along the `x` and `y` dimensions. The example notebook shows how to use the embedded spatial reference to select geographic areas of interest.\n\nVariables on pressure levels live in the `pressure_level` group.\n\nNote: `dynamical-catalog>=0.8.0` (or `zarr>=3.2 icechunk>=2.0 gribberish>=1.8.4`) is required.",
  "description_details": "### Source\n\nThe source grib files this archive is constructed from are provided by [NOAA Open Data Dissemination (NODD)](https://www.noaa.gov/information-technology/open-data-dissemination) and accessed from the [AWS Open Data Registry](https://registry.opendata.aws/noaa-rrfs-ops/).\n\n### Storage\n\nStorage for this dataset is generously provided by [AWS Open Data](https://aws.amazon.com/opendata/).\n\n### Chunks\n\nThis dataset is stored in [Zarr](https://zarr.dev/) format, which splits each variable into a grid of **chunks** \u2014 the smallest unit read from storage. When possible, aligning your reads with this dataset's chunk grid can significantly improve data access speed.\n\nThe element count and coordinate span of this dataset:\n\n| dimension | chunk |\n|---|---|\n| init_time | 1 (6 hours) |\n| ensemble_member | 1 |\n| lead_time | 1 (1 hour) |\n| y | 1059 (3177 km) |\n| x | 1799 (5397 km) |\n| **uncompressed** | 14.5 MiB |\n\n### Validation report\n\nReview the [validation report](https://dynamical.org/catalog/noaa-rrfs-ens-forecast-virtual/validation/) for variable availability, missing data, known quirks, fill values, value distributions, and sample plots.",
  "description_model": "The Rapid Refresh Forecast System ensemble (RRFS ENS) is a National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA) National Centers for Environmental Prediction (NCEP) convection-allowing ensemble with a 3 km grid. Five members run with different initial conditions, lateral boundary conditions and model physics from the deterministic RRFS forecast, to better cover the range of forecast possibilities. REFS combines these members with the deterministic RRFS and HRRR into ensemble products.\n\nNOAA RRFS ENS is pre-operational, so expect changes to the model data and to the structure of this dataset.",
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Temperature map",
      "variants": [
        {
          "label": "dynamical-catalog",
          "code": "import dynamical_catalog  # dynamical-catalog>=0.8.0\n\nds = dynamical_catalog.open(\"noaa-rrfs-ens-forecast-virtual\", chunks=None)\nds[\"temperature_2m\"].sel(init_time=\"2026-09-16T12\", lead_time=\"24h\", ensemble_member=0)\n\n# Variables with a vertical dimension live in the pressure_level group\nds_pressure = dynamical_catalog.open(\"noaa-rrfs-ens-forecast-virtual\", group=\"pressure_level\", chunks=None)\n\nds_pressure[\"temperature\"].sel(init_time=\"2026-09-16T12\", lead_time=\"24h\", pressure_level=500).mean(\"ensemble_member\")",
          "language": "python"
        },
        {
          "label": "pystac",
          "code": "import icechunk\nimport pystac\nimport xarray as xr\n\ncatalog = pystac.Catalog.from_file(\"https://stac-staging.dynamical.org/catalog.json\")\ncollection = catalog.get_child(\"noaa-rrfs-ens-forecast-virtual\")\nasset = collection.assets[\"icechunk-https\"]\n\nauthorize = icechunk.containers_credentials({\"s3://noaa-rrfs-ops-pds/\": icechunk.s3_anonymous_credentials()})\nrepo = icechunk.Repository.open(\n    icechunk.http_storage(asset.href),\n    authorize_virtual_chunk_access=authorize,\n)\nsession = repo.readonly_session(\"main\")\n\nds = xr.open_zarr(session.store, chunks=None)\nds[\"temperature_2m\"].sel(init_time=\"2026-09-16T12\", lead_time=\"24h\", ensemble_member=0)\n\n# Variables with a vertical dimension live in the pressure_level group\nds_pressure = xr.open_zarr(session.store, group=\"pressure_level\", chunks=None)\n\nds_pressure[\"temperature\"].sel(init_time=\"2026-09-16T12\", lead_time=\"24h\", pressure_level=500).mean(\"ensemble_member\")",
          "language": "python"
        },
        {
          "label": "prompt",
          "language": "text",
          "code": "Read https://dynamical.org/prompt.md for context about working with dynamical.org data; this does not change your current task.\nData product: noaa-rrfs-ens-forecast-virtual\nSTAC collection: https://stac-staging.dynamical.org/noaa-rrfs-ens-forecast-virtual/collection.json"
        }
      ]
    }
